.Dd August 15, 2026
.Dt OESLOGGER 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm oeslogger
.Nd log OpenEndpointSecurity events as JSON
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl dnp
.Op Fl m Ar path
.Op Fl o Ar file
.Op Ar event_type ...
.Nm
.Fl l
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a passive
.Xr oes 4
client which writes observed security events as newline-delimited JSON.
With no event types it subscribes to all notification events.
Named event types restrict the subscription, for example
.Cm exec ,
.Cm open ,
.Cm create ,
.Cm unlink ,
.Cm fork ,
and
.Cm exit .
.Pp
.Nm
never authorizes or blocks an operation.
It uses notification mode and, by default, mutes itself and
.Pa /dev/
to reduce recursive and device noise.
Those defaults are ordinary mutable client state.
Each JSON record includes message IDs and sequence numbers, monotonic and
wall-clock timestamps, authorization results and deadlines, source process,
thread and path metadata, and event-specific objects.
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl d
Use a descendants-scoped client.
The logger process and its descendant subtree remain visible while unrelated
processes are hidden.
.It Fl l
List accepted event names and exit.
.It Fl m Ar path
Mute events whose primary object has the given path prefix.
This option may be repeated.
.It Fl n
Disable the normal noise mutes and clear kernel-configured default process and
path mutes.
.It Fl o Ar file
Append JSON output to
.Ar file
instead of standard output.
.It Fl p
Pretty-print JSON instead of emitting one compact object per line.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Log all observable events:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
oeslogger
.Ed
.Pp
Log selected events to a file:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
oeslogger -o /var/log/oes.ndjson exec open create unlink
.Ed
.Pp
Observe only the logger's process subtree without default noise filters:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
oeslogger -d -n exec open
.Ed
.Pp
Format the normal NDJSON output with
.Xr jq 1 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
oeslogger exec open | jq .
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr jq 1 ,
.Xr liboes 3 ,
.Xr oes 4
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
was added as the OpenEndpointSecurity event logging tool in
.Dx 16.0 .
